            <ArticleTitle>[EFFICACY OF WELDING TECHNOLOGY AS A PRINCIPAL METHOD OF DISSECTION AND HEMOSTASIS IN ENDOCRINAL SURGERY].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>45-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Today in the clinic all surgical interventions on endocrinal organs are conducted, using welding technology. Comparative analysis of the operative interventions efficacy, performed applying a standard method (control group) and using welding technology (the main group), was conducted. Performance of operations, using electric welding technologies have permitted to reduce the operative intervention duration by 20 - 30%, the blood loss volume--by 30 - 50%, a postoperative pain syndrome severity and the analgetics expense--by 20%, a postoperative stationary treatment duration--by 1-2 days.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
